1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,000
== Official || kisskh.asia - kissasia.co || ==

2
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,480
You threw away my ring, didn't you?

3
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,879
So that ring matters more than me?

4
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:06,360
You fell for your mother's trick.

5
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,960
This was your plan, wasn't it?

6
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,920
I'd never scheme against you.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,960
You're so full of it!

8
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:15,200
- Huh?
- That's enough. Mom! Stop it!

9
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:19,520
I'm Gingkamol, Runchlaphat's mother.
A show, you say?

10
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,880
I just want her to know that

11
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,240
loving someone

12
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:29,280
shouldn't come at the cost of breaking

13
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,040
a mother's heart.

14
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:35,640
Guys, have you seen
Real Talk With Moms yet?

15
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,680
Oh. I only saw bits of it.

16
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,000
Our boss's mother was on it, right?

17
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:44,920
Yeah. I tell you, this is a big deal.

18
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,760
Hey. I think what she said
was great, though.

19
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,080
She seemed like a very open-minded mother.

20
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,400
That's why it's shady.

21
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,960
Smart people imply things
instead of being direct,

22
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,040
leaving the audience to figure it out.

23
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:05,920
"Some people use love to gain control,

24
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,479
not to understand."

25
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,520
Our boss's mother said it herself.

26
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,880
Who does that remind you of?

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,680
You don't have to answer that.

28
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,600
But just look at the comments.

29
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,120
The whole country knows.

30
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,280
It's their family's business, though.

31
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,680
You could say that.

32
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:32,240
But for someone like her,
it stops being a private matter.

33
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,280
Our boss chose her wife

34
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:37,000
and let her mother go on the show and cry.

35
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,240
If it were me,
of course I'd choose my mother.

36
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,640
You only have one mother, after all.

37
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:44,760
Am I right?

38
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,160
Runch!

39
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,000
Morning.

40
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:00,440
I took a beach trip,
so I bought you some desserts.

41
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,560
I'll leave them in the coffee room

42
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,400
so everyone can enjoy them.

43
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,440
Runch, wait.

44
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,600
You shouldn't go in there yet.

45
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,400
Why not?

46
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:20,240
Some people, huh? When they're in love,

47
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,400
they forget everything else,

48
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,520
even those who raised them.

49
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,840
What?

50
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,880
I just feel bad for her mother.

51
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:35,400
A good person like her is hurt

52
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,760
because her daughter
chose the wrong person.

53
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,200
Are you done, Utt?

54
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,720
You don't know me

55
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,400
or the relationship I have with my mother.

56
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:58,560
You have no right to criticize me
over my private life.

57
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,160
Why not, Boss?

58
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,280
I'm just repeating what I heard.

59
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,720
Your mother said it herself.

60
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,840
Everybody who heard her could tell

61
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,960
that you chose your wife over your mother.

62
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,320
Or did I get it wrong?

63
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,440
If you say another word,

64
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,440
I'll sue you for defamation.

65
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,480
It's time to work.

66
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:30,240
I hope you can do your job as well

67
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,440
as you gossip.

68
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,520
Next time,

69
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,560
if you want to talk about me,

70
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:45,880
why don't you say it to my face?

71
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,400
Runch, Are you okay?

72
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:17,920
I'm okay.

73
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,080
What's wrong with Utt?

74
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:24,400
He's acted this way many times.

75
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,760
He doesn't seem to like you very much,

76
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,080
even though you're his boss.

77
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,320
I never cared to find out why.

78
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,680
He's nobody important to me.

79
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:42,720
Whatever he thinks, says, or does,

80
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,280
let's just let him be.

81
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:51,280
Hey, Utt. Calm down. Don't be so mad.

82
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,320
- I hate her.
- You're doing too much.

83
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,320
I'm not. I don't like her.

84
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,720
I haven't for a while now.
I just can't stand her.

85
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,760
What's wrong with you?

86
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:02,160
She never did anything to you.
You always started it.

87
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,920
Mind your own business!

88
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,560
Hey, Utt. If you keep taking it out on me,
I'm done talking to you.

89
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:11,680
You freaks… One day I'll get you back.

90
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:19,960
Sorry,

91
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,720
Ms. Peeracha isn't available
for an interview.

92
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,960
If you have any concerns,
please send us an email.

93
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:30,720
Yes. But we'd rather not comment on that.

94
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,120
Thank you.

95
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,560
Sorry,

96
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:38,920
Ms. Peeracha has no plans
to speak to the media.

97
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:44,160
What happened?
Why are they calling us nonstop?

98
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:48,720
It's the press, Ms. Neen. Reporters
and online content creators.

99
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,280
From so many agencies too.

100
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,880
The media?

101
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,320
But why?

102
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,880
Well…

103
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:59,120
It's about Mrs. Gingkamol
being on that show.

104
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:03,280
They wanted to interview you about…

105
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,440
your family's relationship.

106
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,400
Are you okay, Neen?

107
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,160
I'm okay.

108
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,520
It's chaos over here, though.

109
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,720
The press won't stop calling.

110
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,280
They're calling you?

111
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:32,679
Yeah. They want to interview me
about your mother being on that show.

112
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,880
I didn't think

113
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,520
this would cause so much trouble for you.

114
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,360
It's a really big deal, though.

115
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,559
It's like everybody's so ready to judge us

116
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,760
without knowing the full story.

117
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,960
I'm really upset about what she did.

118
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,360
No matter how hurt or sad she is,

119
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,840
she has no right to tell anyone
about our private matters

120
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,680
and cause you trouble as a result.

121
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,440
I'm sorry.

122
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,160
It's okay.

123
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:06,720
I'm happy to hear
that you're siding with me.

124
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,760
Well, I'm not happy at all.

125
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,960
Oh, Runch.

126
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,360
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

127
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,440
I would've made you dinner.

128
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,120
Why did you do it?

129
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,160
What did I do?

130
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:29,160
You went on that show
and said all those things.

131
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,640
I didn't do anything, Runch.

132
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:35,080
They wanted me on the show
for an interview, so I said yes.

133
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:37,200
It's not like I begged them to go.

134
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,720
Didn't you think there'd be consequences?

135
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,000
I simply said how I felt.

136
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,360
I didn't slander your wife.

137
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:48,280
I didn't even mention her name once.

138
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,760
People just took it the wrong way.

139
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,680
Well, your words

140
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:56,000
made the whole country see it that way.

141
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,920
See what?

142
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,440
That Neen's the one
who took me away from you.

143
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:06,120
- Or will you deny it?
- I never said that.

144
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,320
But you knew full well

145
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:11,400
how the viewers would think.

146
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:15,200
Runch. I'm a mother.

147
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:17,760
I have the right to express
my feelings as a mother.

148
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:22,360
I was hurt. I was sad.

149
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,240
So I gave them my side of the story.

150
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,400
What about Neen's side?

151
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,120
Neen never said anything.

152
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,760
She never defended herself.

153
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:36,400
But today, she has to face it all

154
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,560
just because of your words.

155
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,640
Would things have ended up like this

156
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,000
if she'd stayed out of our lives?

157
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,040
Mom!

158
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,160
Her coming into my life

159
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:48,520
doesn't mean she took anything from you.

160
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,000
It means I chose her.

161
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,720
And you saying all of that

162
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,000
didn't help protect your daughter at all.

163
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,600
Instead, it hurt the person
your daughter loves.

164
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,200
If you choose to keep this up,

165
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
I'll have to decide

166
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,160
who I'm going to defend.

167
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,040
Runch, Runch!

168
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,880
Runch! Runch!

169
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,240
Runch…

170
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,280
Neen,

171
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,640
Did you see the news about
your mother-in-law on TV?

172
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,480
It's becoming a big deal.

173
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,280
I saw that it's trending.

174
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,160
It's not just trending.

175
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:14,120
The news has reached the food industry
and investors too.

176
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,360
I'm worried it'll affect your reputation.

177
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,320
And the restaurant you're opening

178
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,040
will be affected too.

179
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,520
As your brother,

180
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:31,040
I'll be honest with you.
You need to do something.

181
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:36,400
But if I say anything now,
it'll only look like I'm making excuses.

182
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:38,760
But if you stay quiet,

183
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,800
it'll seem like
you're admitting it's true.

184
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,320
I get it, but this kind of story
only stays trending

185
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,760
when people get emotional.

186
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,880
The more I respond,
the more it'll spread like wildfire.

187
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,680
People won't listen to reason.

188
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:54,320
They'll only side with
whoever seems more like the victim.

189
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:57,120
So, I figured I'd just stay quiet
until the news

190
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:59,040
eventually dies down.

191
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
I understand where you're coming from.

192
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,160
But I have to protect
our family's business too.

193
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,200
I understand.

194
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,920
Fine. If something happens,
I'll take responsibility for it.

195
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,600
You sure you can do that?

196
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:18,000
Yeah. I am.

197
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:23,320
I have news about Peeracha the socialite
and her wife.

198
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,360
Surely this story
will get your show's rating

199
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:28,640
even higher than
that "Selfless Mother" video.

200
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,600
Sorry I'm late.

201
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,200
Let's get started, Mrs. Piyarat.

202
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:48,760
You said your son and your daughter-in-law

203
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,520
kicked you out of the house?

204
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,240
Yes.

205
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,760
I never thought

206
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:56,960
that my own son would do that to me.

207
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,680
He and his wife asked me
to transfer my house to them.

208
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:04,960
He promised he'd take care of me
and never leave me.

209
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:07,360
And I believed him.

210
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,920
Once the house was in his name,

211
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,760
everything changed.

212
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:16,400
He told me it's his house,

213
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:19,200
and I could stay

214
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:21,280
only if I followed his rules.

215
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,040
In the end,

216
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,560
he kicked me out of there.

217
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:34,840
When you signed the house over,
did you make any other agreements?

218
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:38,440
For example, a right to live there
or any conditions regarding your care?

219
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:40,280
Not at all.

220
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,400
I only signed it over

221
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:44,840
because I trusted
he'd be good to his mother.

222
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,440
You know, some people even think

223
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:51,080
that surely,
I pressured my own son somehow,

224
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:53,080
so much so he kicked me out.

225
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:58,480
But nobody asked me how I felt.

226
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:02,320
This isn't your fault, ma'am.

227
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:05,920
And your son and his wife
can't treat you however they want

228
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,680
just because you trust him.

229
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:11,960
We'll do our best to provide you
with legal support

230
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,840
and make sure you regain your rights.

231
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,520
Thank you.

232
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,960
Excuse me.

233
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,680
Can I talk to you for a moment?

234
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,960
It's about your case.

235
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:36,960
Sure.

236
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,440
She wants a different lawyer?

237
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:45,160
But I was just talking to Mrs. Piyarat.

238
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,320
Things were going so well.

239
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,080
I'm sure there's been a misunderstanding.

240
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,400
There hasn't.

241
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:56,040
She had Mr. Utt call me just a moment ago.

242
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:57,760
Mr. Utt?

243
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,680
Mrs. Piyarat

244
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:02,680
wants Mr. Utt to handle this case
in your place.

245
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,560
May I ask why?

246
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:10,120
It's because of the news about you.

247
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,440
Mrs. Piyarat is scared

248
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:17,360
that you'll side with her son
and daughter-in-law,

249
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:19,000
and lose her the case.

250
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,160
Even though I always took her side

251
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,640
for this case?

252
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,400
I know.

253
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,680
And I trust your professionalism.

254
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,880
But some clients

255
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:39,240
just want to be very sure.

256
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,800
What about the company?

257
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,480
Are you sure about me?

258
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,080
If I wasn't,

259
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,720
I wouldn't be speaking to you directly.

260
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,440
Understood.

261
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:01,760
I'll follow the procedure
and transfer the case to Mr. Utt.

262
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,280
I'm sorry

263
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,520
that your private life
is affecting your work.

264
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:11,680
I'm not sorry.

265
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:14,079
I'm just a bit disappointed

266
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:18,280
that rumors hold more weight than facts.

267
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,880
Here are all the files for the case.

268
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:38,560
Please do your best in this case.

269
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:41,000
Save Mrs. Piyarat.

270
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:45,920
Got it. I'll do my best.

271
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,040
I'm sorry, Boss.

272
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,320
For what?

273
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,200
I'm feeling as if

274
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:04,160
I'm taking your work away from you.

275
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:10,720
There's no need to apologize.

276
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:15,320
It's up to the client to decide
who they're comfortable with.

277
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:19,520
A lawyer's job is to build
the strongest case,

278
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,840
not to keep all the work for themselves.

279
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,240
I hope you won't disappoint the client.

280
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:34,760
Here.

281
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,720
Did you order anything yet?

282
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,280
I was waiting for you to do it.

283
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,520
Sure.

284
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:47,720
Can we get a menu?

285
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:50,480
Isn't that the girl in the news?

286
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,840
Yeah. She chose her wife over her mom.

287
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:57,520
There's been a new update. Apparently,

288
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,920
it's because her wife is richer.

289
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,400
So she's a gold-digger.

290
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,840
Neen.

291
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:06,880
No.

292
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:11,480
Leave them be. Let's eat somewhere else.

293
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:17,160
Fine.

294
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:18,760
‪Let's go.

295
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:27,320
Look. They must feel embarrassed.
That's why they're leaving.

296
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,640
- Famous people, huh?
- Hey, just eat.

297
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,280
Excuse me.

298
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,040
If you keep talking that way,

299
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:47,200
then let me make this clear.

300
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:51,480
You can expect a court summons
for defamation.

301
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:08,520
I'm sorry I killed the vibe.

302
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,280
We went from a nice restaurant
to instant noodles at home.

303
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,280
It's okay. The noodles are great too.

304
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:18,640
Hey,

305
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:22,160
you were a total badass, by the way.

306
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,120
How so?

307
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,400
Well, it was when you said,

308
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,680
"Keep talking and expect a court summons."

309
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,240
You're still in the mood to laugh?

310
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,920
Of course.

311
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,640
It's just gossip.

312
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,280
I don't let it get to me.

313
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,720
It's nonsense.

314
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
But I don't think…

315
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:54,040
- Yeah?
- …we should let it slide,

316
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,360
especially now that there are
lots of malicious people

317
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,800
who spread fake news about us.

318
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:05,320
So what are you going to do, Runch?

319
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,720
I don't want to respond emotionally.

320
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:15,800
I don't want you
to explain yourself either.

321
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:22,760
And I definitely won't let anyone
twist the facts about our family

322
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,840
and use them against us.

323
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,400
- You want more?
- No.

324
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:43,480
YOU CAN EARN M POINTS - SCAN YOUR RECEIPTS
OR TELL THE CASHIER YOUR M CARD NUMBER

325
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,920
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

326
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:03,320
I was never angry
or hateful toward anyone.

327
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,600
I just want her to know that

328
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,000
loving someone

329
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:14,920
shouldn't come at the cost

330
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,400
of breaking…

331
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,600
a mother's heart.

332
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:22,960
What we saw was part
of Mrs. Gingkamol's interview.

333
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:26,000
Today, we'd like to hear
Ms. Runchlaphat's side of the story

334
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,960
as a daughter

335
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:30,040
and a wife.

336
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:30,960
Sure.

337
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,480
My mother is a strong woman.

338
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,320
And I'm her daughter.

339
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:48,480
I grew up under a lot of expectations.

340
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,040
I kept hearing, "You must be great."

341
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,720
"You must be capable."

342
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,920
"You must not let your mother down."

343
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,560
That very strength

344
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:02,000
has made me who I am today,

345
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:05,880
and I never denied that fact.

346
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,360
All my life, I've been trying
to overcome the expectations,

347
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:13,640
to overcome the fear

348
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:17,800
that if one day,
I decide to choose my own life,

349
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,960
I'll become a bad daughter.

350
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,920
Today, I've decided to choose love.

351
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:27,640
I know full well I must prove,
more than anyone,

352
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:31,760
that I don't love her
because of her money.

353
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:34,480
And I must prove

354
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,040
that I haven't left anyone behind.

355
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:42,120
My wife and I

356
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:44,960
have chosen to build a life together

357
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:46,760
based on honesty

358
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,880
and mutual responsibility.

359
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:55,240
I came here to say this today
not to win against anyone,

360
00:23:56,480 --> 00:24:00,160
but to stand firm in my own truth.

361
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,600
Runch!

362
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:20,000
You never told me
you were going on that show.

363
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,520
I just wanted to handle it myself.

364
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:27,120
You know, Runch,

365
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:30,280
you couldn't have said it better
for us both.

366
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,720
I was just telling the truth.

367
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:41,120
I'm so proud of you.

368
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:48,480
From now on, no matter what happens,

369
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:51,160
I won't let you face it alone.

370
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,320
Same here.

371
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:57,960
From now on, no matter what we face,
we won't let go of each other's hands.

372
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,160
I have a reward for you.

373
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,360
Right now?

374
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,880
I guarantee you, it'll be yummy.

375
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:11,240
Yummy, you say?

376
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:14,360
Come on.

377
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:28,320
This is what you meant by yummy?

378
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:30,200
Yes.

379
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:40,200
It looks really good. Don't you want it?

380
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,680
- So good.
- Yeah.

381
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:11,640
So yummy.

382
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:19,800
This is the first time
it truly feels like we're on vacation.

383
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:24,640
It's the first time
I don't have to feel guilty

384
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:26,760
about not answering any calls.

385
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:33,600
No checking the news, turning on the TV,
or going on social media.

386
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:37,080
Just us spending time together.

387
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:46,320
This house used to feel
like a battlefield, didn't it?

388
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,320
Yeah.

389
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:55,040
But today, I want it
to really feel like our home.

390
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:59,960
Then, let's not compete with anyone today.

391
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:04,440
There's no need to compete with anyone
or prove anything.

392
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:06,800
All we do is rest.

393
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:37,680
All done!

394
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:38,680
So hot.

395
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,880
- Looks pretty clean to me.
- Yeah.

396
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,720
Where's Runch?

397
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:03,360
Go get her for me now!

398
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:06,880
What is it, Mom?

399
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,080
You turned off your phone.
Didn't want me to call you or what?

400
00:29:11,560 --> 00:29:13,040
We need to talk.

401
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:17,520
Runch and I.

402
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:19,920
Just the two of us.

403
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,720
You think what you did was right?

404
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,960
You went on that show and spoke on TV.

405
00:29:51,040 --> 00:29:53,360
You made it seem like I hurt others,

406
00:29:53,440 --> 00:29:55,800
and I'm the only one who's at fault.

407
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:58,520
Well, you went on that show earlier too.

408
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:02,440
That's different. I was there as a mother.

409
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:06,520
I have the right to express my feelings.
I didn't mention any names.

410
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:08,920
People just took it the wrong way.

411
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:10,800
Sure.

412
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:14,560
They took it the wrong way,

413
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:16,320
as you said.

414
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:18,840
Are you talking back to me?

415
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:21,160
I'm not.

416
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:26,080
I'm just giving you
a taste of your own medicine.

417
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,400
What are you talking about?

418
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:31,960
You made the whole country
feel sorry for you.

419
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:34,440
What about me? Who am I?

420
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:38,040
Now I'm the cruel mother,
the selfish mother.

421
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:40,720
I've become a villain
in my daughter's life!

422
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:44,440
When you gave the interview, you knew
exactly how the viewers would think.

423
00:30:45,040 --> 00:30:47,080
You just chose not to take responsibility.

424
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:48,920
I'm not taking responsibility
for anything!

425
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:53,800
I'm a mother. I can get hurt.

426
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:56,960
I can get sad. Can't I say anything?

427
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,520
You can.

428
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:02,640
But Neen paid the price, not you.

429
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:06,680
Our lives were ruined
because of that woman.

430
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:12,720
Before, I never
had to give any interviews.

431
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:16,680
I never had to feel embarrassed
or cry on TV for anyone's entertainment.

432
00:31:17,280 --> 00:31:19,160
Don't let her hear that.

433
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:22,560
What, are you afraid she'll be upset?
What about me, then?

434
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,640
Can I be upset?

435
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:26,080
Can I feel hurt?

436
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:29,720
Or do I have to be the only one
who's understanding?

437
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,560
Don't forget.

438
00:31:37,040 --> 00:31:38,760
You started it.

439
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:42,160
So don't blame me.

440
00:31:45,120 --> 00:31:47,000
So you really chose her.

441
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,640
You really chose her over me.

442
00:31:58,640 --> 00:32:00,400
I chose my own life.

443
00:32:01,600 --> 00:32:04,720
And I won't let anyone
hurt the one I love.

444
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,200
No one.

445
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:17,040
So from now on,

446
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:19,760
what am I to you?

447
00:32:23,560 --> 00:32:24,520
Am I…

448
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:29,120
not the one you love anymore?

449
00:32:55,760 --> 00:32:57,560
You're still my mother.

450
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:01,560
I love you, Mom.

451
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,560
But there should be boundaries

452
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:12,320
in our relationship,

453
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:18,000
like we're two adults
who respect each other's privacy.

454
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:26,280
Boundaries? Don't sugarcoat it.

455
00:33:30,840 --> 00:33:34,520
In reality, what you're trying to say is…

456
00:33:37,760 --> 00:33:39,000
"From now on,

457
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:43,880
stay the hell out of my life."

458
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:45,120
Isn't that right?

459
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:48,560
Well, if it's not really necessary

460
00:33:50,080 --> 00:33:52,000
or a matter of life and death,

461
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:57,960
then there's no need for you to see me.

462
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:34,480
You don't have to say anything.
I heard everything.

463
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:04,760
We're alone together now.

464
00:35:07,080 --> 00:35:09,440
You don't have to try to be strong.

465
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:26,320
Yeah?

466
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:40,360
I wasn't dragged into this.

467
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:43,240
I chose this.

468
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:49,080
I chose you. I chose us.

469
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:57,560
If today was tiring,

470
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:00,960
we can be tired together.

471
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:03,280
It's okay to win at nothing for one day.

472
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:17,880
I feel so lucky…

473
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:22,040
to have you by my side.

474
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:28,320
Then how about you let me
stay by your side forever?

475
00:37:10,120 --> 00:37:11,800
Did you get any sleep last night?

476
00:37:14,080 --> 00:37:15,240
I did.

477
00:37:16,640 --> 00:37:19,520
I did because you were there by my side.

478
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:29,200
Penny for your thoughts?

479
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:38,040
I'm deciding

480
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:42,080
whether we should leave
what happened as a wound

481
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:46,640
or change it to something better.

482
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:53,680
I want to start a small project.
Something low-key.

483
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:56,240
It doesn't have to be a big deal.

484
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:58,880
Maybe a foundation for children

485
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:01,600
or women

486
00:38:01,680 --> 00:38:03,840
who are rejected by their families

487
00:38:04,520 --> 00:38:06,960
just for being themselves

488
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:08,920
or because of their gender.

489
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:17,080
I don't want anyone to feel
like their love is a crime.

490
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:23,000
That way, our love
won't stay just between us,

491
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:27,040
but we'll get to give our love
to others too.

492
00:38:28,280 --> 00:38:31,480
I don't know how well I'll do it.

493
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:35,360
I just know I don't want to do it alone.

494
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:40,720
Well, have I ever let you?

495
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,800
If the world is cruel to us,

496
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:49,680
we just have to be kind in return.
That's all.

497
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:55,360
How about this? We'll ask Nai for advice

498
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:56,920
about the foundation.

499
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,720
Sounds good.

500
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:03,360
I'm sure he'd be a big help.

501
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:11,040
Absolutely.

502
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:15,480
Our company already owns
a foundation for children in need.

503
00:39:15,560 --> 00:39:18,000
We already have
the infrastructure in place,

504
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:20,280
and our operations are transparent.

505
00:39:22,680 --> 00:39:26,680
Some of the families we've worked with
faced the same issue.

506
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,480
Some children don't lack money.

507
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:31,280
They lack a place where they belong.

508
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:35,000
If you want to start a foundation,

509
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:37,600
it could be a safe space for them.

510
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:41,160
A place where no one judges them.

511
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:43,000
Yeah.

512
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,920
I don't want anyone to feel

513
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:46,880
like they don't belong anywhere.

514
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:51,560
I want to make sure
everything's done properly.

515
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:53,600
I don't want anyone to get hurt,

516
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:55,640
including their families.

517
00:39:57,640 --> 00:39:59,080
My thoughts exactly.

518
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:32,400
- Hello.
- Hello, ma'am.

519
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,960
You work here, right?

520
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:36,040
Yes.

521
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:38,840
You're my boss's mother, right?

522
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:41,240
I work for her.

523
00:40:42,560 --> 00:40:44,200
You recognize me?

524
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:45,600
Of course I do.

525
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:48,120
I just watched the show
where you gave the interview.

526
00:40:50,600 --> 00:40:52,480
I'm on your side, by the way.

527
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:56,160
Really? That's good to hear.

528
00:40:56,840 --> 00:41:00,120
Oh, right.
I bought some food for everyone,

529
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:02,240
but I don't want to bother Runch.

530
00:41:02,320 --> 00:41:03,480
Can you hand it out for me?

531
00:41:03,560 --> 00:41:04,400
Sure.

532
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:08,960
And please don't tell Runch I came here.

533
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:10,880
Why not?

534
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:16,520
I just don't want her
to feel uncomfortable.

535
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:23,040
It's because of the interview
my boss recently gave, right?

536
00:41:23,120 --> 00:41:25,520
That's why you don't want anyone
to know you're here.

537
00:41:35,480 --> 00:41:37,000
It's alright.

538
00:41:38,560 --> 00:41:40,480
I never thought

539
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:43,400
my daughter could be so mad at me.

540
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:49,480
She's always taking her wife's side,

541
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:52,320
like I'm not her mother anymore.

542
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:55,760
Like I'm an outsider
in my own daughter's life.

543
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:08,880
It hurts me so bad.

544
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:11,640
It really does.

545
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:14,840
Everything I did

546
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:17,160
was for my daughter.

547
00:42:17,960 --> 00:42:20,240
Never for myself.

548
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:25,760
I understand.

549
00:42:26,400 --> 00:42:30,440
To a mother, this is something
that hurts deeply.

550
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:36,200
I just didn't want her
to have a difficult life,

551
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:40,400
but in the end,
I'm the one who's at fault.

552
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:52,040
I've known her for so long.

553
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:56,640
She only changed when this person
came into her life.

554
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:08,560
Let me know
if I can help you with anything.

555
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,200
I'm on your side.

556
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:16,680
In that case,

557
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:19,200
can I get your number?

558
00:43:20,520 --> 00:43:21,600
Of course.

559
00:43:23,600 --> 00:43:24,640
I'm Utt, by the way.

560
00:43:25,960 --> 00:43:27,560
I really appreciate it, Utt.

561
00:43:28,160 --> 00:43:32,120
At least some people still listen to me.

562
00:44:08,560 --> 00:44:10,200
What about you, Ms. Runchlaphat?

563
00:44:10,280 --> 00:44:11,920
What do you like about Ms. Peeracha?

564
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:13,240
1 YEAR AGO

565
00:44:17,040 --> 00:44:20,880
She's very… truthful.

566
00:44:22,640 --> 00:44:24,760
She stays true to her feelings,

567
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:26,360
to others…

568
00:44:28,320 --> 00:44:31,400
and also to the feeling of love.

569
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:34,200
At work,

570
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:36,920
I've met people who are eloquent,

571
00:44:37,600 --> 00:44:39,720
people who are confident,

572
00:44:40,960 --> 00:44:44,080
and lots of people who are skilled.

573
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:47,640
But Neen is the only one

574
00:44:49,280 --> 00:44:51,920
who's not afraid to say,
"I can't take it."

575
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:03,160
And she doesn't say it
to ask for anything.

576
00:45:04,480 --> 00:45:09,160
She only says it
to let me know she really can't take it.

577
00:45:12,720 --> 00:45:14,320
I like how she doesn't

578
00:45:15,160 --> 00:45:16,720
try to beat anyone,

579
00:45:18,400 --> 00:45:22,200
but rather, she tries
to be honest with herself.

580
00:45:24,480 --> 00:45:26,840
And so, she taught me that

581
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:30,360
love isn't about arguments

582
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:36,320
or proving who's right.

583
00:45:37,680 --> 00:45:39,400
It's about choosing.

584
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:42,080
Choosing to stay by each other's side,

585
00:45:43,200 --> 00:45:45,680
even when nothing is clear.

586
00:45:53,520 --> 00:45:55,280
That's why I chose Neen.

587
00:45:57,320 --> 00:46:00,400
Not because you are perfect,

588
00:46:02,440 --> 00:46:04,400
but because

589
00:46:05,480 --> 00:46:07,480
you are the truth

590
00:46:08,760 --> 00:46:11,880
I want to protect for the rest of my life.

591
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:48,760
I did everything for you.

592
00:46:48,840 --> 00:46:52,960
But in the end, I wasn't the one you chose
to stand by.

593
00:46:53,040 --> 00:46:54,240
Runch is done with you.

594
00:46:54,320 --> 00:46:57,200
If she's really
going to let her wife bully me,

595
00:46:57,880 --> 00:46:59,120
then so be it.

596
00:46:59,200 --> 00:47:01,680
To our family. To us.

597
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:06,320
Crazy bitch!

598
00:47:06,400 --> 00:47:08,000
- You bitch, how dare you!
- Stop it!

599
00:47:08,080 --> 00:47:09,840
You had no right to do this to me!

600
00:47:55,360 --> 00:47:57,360
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
